The plate looks like a square side or dinner plate, roughly 24 cm across. In the image it spans about 465 px (from x=140 to x=605), so about 0.052 cm per px. The waffle spans about 335 px, which is roughly 17 cm in diameter. It is about 1.5 cm thick. That gives a volume of π × 8.5² × 1.5 ≈ 340 cm³, but waffles are airy with deep pockets, so I use a density of about 0.35 g/cm³. That gives roughly 120 g, though a round 17 cm waffle usually weighs about 130 g.

Some syrup is visible pooled in the pockets, perhaps 10 g.

